  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging political support to fight tiger and other illegal wildlife trade on the Vietnam-China..border</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to reduce the volume of illegal trade in tigers across the Vietnam-China border through increased Government of Vietnam action to fight illegal wildlife trade. This will be done by: (1) facilitating central and provincial level inter-agency communication and coordination on combating transnational wildlife crimes on the Vietnam-China border; (2) enhancing communications and coordination between relevant agencies in Guangxi (China) and Quang Ninh (Vietnam) province on combating transnational wildlife crimes along their shared border; (3) increasing the attention and response from government of Vietnam on inspection of shipments and related investigations at the Mong Cai border crossing by coordinating and partnering with organizations and agencies working on the other forms of crime in Vietnam; and (4) generating domestic and international media coverage that supports prevention and suppression of transnational wildlife crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
